    "page": 5,
    "text": " How do you hear?\nYou don’t need to memorize any\nof these names, except cochlea\n\n Waves of vibration in the air\n  arrive at your external ear,\n  then travel inward to your\n  inner ear, a part called the\n  cochlea, the part that sends\n  signals to your brain that say\n what frequencies are in the\n  sound.",
