    "text": "Vocal folds\n\n• Your vocal folds are muscles that are\n about 1 cm in length and 1 mm in\n  height.\n• Muscle has mass and stiffness\n• Using about 10 other muscles hooked\n  to the bones/cartilages of the housing\n  of the folds, we can stretch them                                          How/Why do they vibrate? making them stiffer or bunching them\n making them effectively heavier.                                                                               If we take air into our lungs, and close the\n• Why?                                               vocal folds, a lot of pressure builds beneath\n     • Singing!                                    them, and if the pressure is high enough, it\n     • In English: Conveying questions, mistrust,    blows them apart, and there is airflow\n     degree of belief, surprise, emotion, etc.!                                               between them. But just like a curtain in a\n     • In tone language: meanings of words!!!!                                                     shower, the airflow sucks the vocal folds\n• We call the vibration frequency of vocal   back in, and the air pressure below blows\n  folds pitch, F0, fundamental frequency.  them apart again, and this repeats 100’s of\n                                                   time per second. The suction force is called\n                                                     the Bernoulli force which lifts airpalnes!",
